CORE
main.sh

^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^\[shell-arithmetic\.1\] file main.sh line 3 value of x is an integer constant in arithmetic expansion \(other values are not supported\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
A variable whose value is not an integer constant is an error in dash
and evaluated recursively in bash; it is reported rather than given
either meaning.
